Within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, we investigate the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, taking into account existing experimental data from Belle and LHCb. By analyzing $B 	o K^{(*)} 	au  ar{
u}$ decays, we derive constraints on the leptoquark's mass and coupling, and subsequently, we estimate the branching ratio and kinematic variables for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au \  ar{
u}$ decays. Future $B$ factory experiments will provide crucial insights into the $U_1$ leptoquark model's validity.
